Ladybird now places an empty inline box on its line in quirks and
limited-quirks mode too, and takes only its line height away under
the line-height quirk. Blink does the same: LogicalLineBuilder::
HandleOpenTag() still places the box of an item that IsEmptyItem(),
and only skips its text metrics. WebKit places the box and decides
in InlineQuirks::inlineBoxAffectsLineBox() if it affects the line
box. Gecko places the span, and zeroes its line height through
zeroEffectiveSpanBox in nsLineLayout::VerticalAlignFrames(), which also
counts a margin, where Ladybird, Blink, and WebKit don’t.

Chrome 157.0.8103.79, Firefox 151.0, and Playwright’s WebKit 26.5 ran
the cases of the two tests added here. Ladybird gives what Chrome and
WebKit give in every case. Firefox puts an empty box’s zero-height rect
at the baseline, and counts a box with a margin.
